{"arrivo":"cs","origine":"ine-pro","origine_nome":"Proto-Indo-European","n":11,"n_alternative":3,"parole":[{"parola":"liknavý","pos":"adj","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"no","significato":"dilatory","termine_origine":"*leykʷ-","catena":[{"codice":"ine-pro","nome":"Proto-Indo-European","termine":"*leykʷ-","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"ine-pro","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"Inherited from Old Czech liknavý, ultimately from Proto-Indo-European *leykʷ-."},{"parola":"lákat","pos":"verb","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"no","significato":"to attract (to arouse interest)","termine_origine":"*leh₂-","catena":[{"codice":"ine-pro","nome":"Proto-Indo-European","termine":"*leh₂-","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"ine-pro","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"From Proto-Indo-European *leh₂- (“to be concealed”)."},{"parola":"odtažitý","pos":"adj","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"ereditato","incerta":"no","significato":"abstract (detached from reality)","termine_origine":"*tengʰ-","catena":[{"codice":"ine-pro","nome":"Proto-Indo-European","termine":"*tengʰ-","categoria":"ereditato"}],"lontana":"ine-pro","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"From odtáhnout (\"to drag away\"), itself derived from od- + táhnout (\"to drag\"). Ultimately from Proto-Indo-European *tengʰ- (“to pull”)."},{"parola":"povidla","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"sì","motivo_incerta":"Possibly","significato":"plum stew, powidl","termine_origine":"*peu-","catena":[{"codice":"ine-pro","nome":"Proto-Indo-European","termine":"*peu-","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"ine-pro","ambiti":["cucina"],"via":"","testo":"Possibly from vít (“to wind, roll”), meaning “something produced by stirring, mixing of a boiled fruit juice”. An alternate etymology derives the word ultimately from Proto-Indo-European *peu- (“to cleanse, purify”), in the sense “purified concoction”."},{"parola":"strdí","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"no","significato":"honey","termine_origine":"*ser-","catena":[{"codice":"ine-pro","nome":"Proto-Indo-European","termine":"*ser-","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"ine-pro","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"Related to Proto-Indo-European *ser-."},{"parola":"váhat","pos":"verb","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"no","significato":"to hesitate","termine_origine":"*weǵʰ-","catena":[{"codice":"ine-pro","nome":"Proto-Indo-European","termine":"*weǵʰ-","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"ine-pro","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"Of a class of words related to \"weighing\" or \"considering,\" such as vážit (“to weigh”), vážný (“serious”), vyvážit (“to balance”), all ultimately from Proto-Indo-European *weǵʰ- (“to convey, transport”)."},{"parola":"vážný","pos":"adj","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"no","significato":"serious","termine_origine":"*weǵʰ-","catena":[{"codice":"ine-pro","nome":"Proto-Indo-European","termine":"*weǵʰ-","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"ine-pro","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"Of a class of words related to \"weighing\" or \"considering,\" such as vážit (“to weigh”), all ultimately from Proto-Indo-European *weǵʰ- (“to convey, transport”)."},{"parola":"čára","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"sì","motivo_incerta":"Possibly; Probably","significato":"line","termine_origine":"*(s)ker-","catena":[{"codice":"ine-pro","nome":"Proto-Indo-European","termine":"*(s)ker-","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"ine-pro","ambiti":["scienza"],"via":"","testo":"Probably derived from čáry (“magic”), čarovat (“to conjure”), meaning a magical line, e.g. the delineation of a magic circle. Possibly connected also with Proto-Indo-European *(s)ker- (“to cut”). First attested in the 14th century."},{"parola":"bedla","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"sì","motivo_incerta":"Possibly; or from; either","significato":"name of several genera of fungi from the family Agaricaceae","termine_origine":"*bʰew-","catena":[{"codice":"ine-pro","nome":"Proto-Indo-European","termine":"*bʰew-","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"ine-pro","ambiti":[],"via":"","alternative":[{"codice":"pl","nome":"Polish","termine":"bedła","categoria":"prestito"},{"codice":"sla-pro","nome":"Proto-Slavic","termine":"*bъdla","categoria":"ereditato"},{"codice":"sla-pro","nome":"Proto-Slavic","termine":"*bъdlo","categoria":"ereditato"},{"codice":"ine-pro","nome":"Proto-Indo-European","termine":"*bʰew-","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"testo":"The word was introduced into biology by botanist Jan Svatopluk Presl in 1846, who borrowed it either from Polish bedła, Polish bedłka or from some Czech dialect. Comes from Proto-Slavic *bъdla or Proto-Slavic *bъdlo. Compare Lithuanian budė̃ (“sponge, polypore”), both possibly from Proto-Indo-Europe"},{"parola":"jed","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"sì","motivo_incerta":"either","significato":"poison","termine_origine":"*ēd-","catena":[{"codice":"ine-pro","nome":"Proto-Indo-European","termine":"*ēd-","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"ine-pro","ambiti":[],"via":"","alternative":[{"codice":"sla-pro","nome":"Proto-Slavic","termine":"*ědъ","categoria":"ereditato"},{"codice":"ine-pro","nome":"Proto-Indo-European","termine":"*ēd-","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"goh","nome":"Old High German","termine":"eitar","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"ine-pro","nome":"Proto-Indo-European","termine":"*oid-","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"testo":"Inherited from Old Czech jěd, from Proto-Slavic *ědъ; either from *ěsti (“to eat”), from Proto-Indo-European *ēd-, or related to Old High German eitar (“pus”), from Proto-Indo-European *oid-."},{"parola":"plískanice","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"sì","motivo_incerta":"either","significato":"sleet","termine_origine":"","catena":[{"codice":"ine-pro","nome":"Proto-Indo-European","termine":"","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"ine-pro","ambiti":[],"via":"","alternative":[{"codice":"sla-pro","nome":"Proto-Slavic","termine":"*pluskari","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"ine-pro","nome":"Proto-Indo-European","termine":"","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"testo":"From plískán + -ice, from the verb plískat, from Proto-Slavic *pluskari (“slapping”), either ultimately from Proto-Indo-European *pleh₂-u-d- (“to clap the hands”), from *pleh₂-u-h₂- (“palm of the hand”), from *pleh₂- (“flat”); or simply onomatopoeic (compare *pleskati (“to splash”))."}]}